    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0556" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg476"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1112/62: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-10T17:00:00+01:00">October 10, 1936—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 10—3:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>431. In introducing the report and resolutions of the Second Committee<anchor
                        n="44" xml:id="d392-f1"/> which were approved by the Assembly this afternoon
                    in substantially the form reported in the Consulate’s telegrams 426, October 9,
                    8 p.m., and 425, October 9, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="45" xml:id="d392-f2"/> Spinasse
                    made a strong plea for the removal of the obstacles to trade.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d392-f1" n="44" xml:id="d392-f1-content">
                <p>Adopted October 9; see League of Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Official
                        Journal</hi>, Special Supplement No. 157, pp. 86 and 97.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d392-f2" n="45" xml:id="d392-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
